{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/23260-cult-of-the-werewolf","id":23260,"title":"Cult of the Werewolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-04T12:19:33-08:00","id":23260,"title":"Cult of the Werewolf","content":"Inspired by Mummy: the Curse, I became fascinated with the idea of cults in the World of Darkness. Looking through the God-Machine Chronicles, I started to wonder about who these people in cults are and that they should have a book to themselves. Well since that's probably not going to happen I thought why not make my own. While doing a little research I began thinking about what if the other beasts in the world had their own cults and what would they look like.<br /> <br /> I started with werewolves, since they are traditionally a tribal people with a history and culture similar to mummies. I wrote a rough outline for what a werewolf cult would look like and how it would operate. Problem is I'm no expert on werewolf (having only read the book once before). So I was wondering if everything below is accurate.<br /> <br /> Note: This is a first draft and nothing below is indicative of anything other than intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Werewolf cults are rare. Werewolves traditionally have their own tribes to provide them support. But they aren't unheard of. These rare tribal cults are made up of the spirit touched, those rare people that have witnessed a spirit exerting its influence on the world. The have no idea what they've just seen but the wolves hunting the creature seem to. Maybe these witnesses just walk away, constantly saying to themselves that what they saw wasn't real. They go through their whole lives with a nigling doubt that something in the world is very wrong. Many are institutionalized because of it. But a few think that, maybe it was real. And an even fewer number pursue that thought to find the truth. These are the people that make up a werewolf cult.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The people that make up the cult are generally curiouser than most. They have a belief that the world is bigger than it seems. The cultists need a large willpower to resist the lunacy that comes with witnessing a werewolf. You also need a lot of balls to actually pursue a giant skulking wolf beast chasing a creature from another realm. When they do find the wolf they are usually curious, if they aren't killed to protect the secret. A large portion also have very few ties to a culture and or a community. So when they observe the tight knit workings of the tribe or lodge, they want to become a part of it. All this culminates in a small group of humans that follow and worship the same traditions and legends the werewolves do under the tutelage of their patron wolf.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">What would a werewolf need a cult for though? A werewolf has her pack mates, a stronger bond than family. Well that's just the thing. The werewolf is a gap between humanity and spirit. Some crave the mortal world but they can never truly leave the world of spirits. So it would be tempting to surround yourself with people that take an interest in the spirits. These cultists worship you as a deity or maybe you just help them believe that they're not going crazy. Whatever the reason, they need you. The problems arise when you start to depend on them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">But how does the tribe react when they find out about these cults. Poorly, the be blunt about it. If the werewolf is lucky, she will just be abandoned by her pack or tribe and become a Ghost Wolf.</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> If she is unlucky however, her cult will be destroyed by the leaders of the tribe. Outsiders are not usually welcomed to learn about the werewolf traditions unless they are specifically touched by the wolf blood. Otherwise, they are people trying to usurp tradition and ritual for their own gain. A werewolf that is open about their cult, probably won't live long.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A werewolf cult is small, with the werewolf at the center acting as spiritual leader. Their goal is to guide their followers in the ways of the spirits and teach them about the greater cosmology around them.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Thoughts, comments, complaints?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T12:25:40-08:00","id":23261,"title":"","content":"Blasphemies has a chapter on cults, including cults devoted to werewolves, I should note, and some packs and wolf-blooded families are essentially cults themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T12:28:09-08:00","id":23264,"title":"","content":"I like it, though I must admit it feels weird to have anything in World of Darkness that is pro-werewolf.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I'm just thinking of Exalted, but I could see how a cult that worshiped a werewolf could somehow give it essence, or at least fuel a loci. It would give werewolves some incentive to try and start one, though, and I'm not sure if that's a good idea (once the mechanics are available then everyone would just tack on a couple cult merit points).<br /> <br /> I've actually had something like it, the NPC werewolf is a Bale Hound of Pride, and has a cult of personality built around her that gives her a lot of power in the city we play in and its scientific community. That's more of an evil, artificially created cult though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T15:46:01-08:00","id":23357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/23260-cult-of-the-werewolf?p=23261#post23261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blasphemies has a chapter on cults, including cults devoted to werewolves, I should note, and some packs and wolf-blooded families are essentially cults themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will definitely have to pick that up sometime.<br /> <br /> My idea is focused more on the mortals than the other supernaturals and how they would become part of these cults and why they choose to stay. Probably not very apparent in the little blurb I wrote up as it focuses on the werewolf but that's where I want to focus on. Though I probably should think up ideas on why supernaturals would join a cult. Lots to think about now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could see how a cult that worshiped a werewolf could somehow give it essence, or at least fuel a loci. </div> </div> </div>I would have to look it up to see if that's accurate (or someone could tell me). But yes that would be very exploitable by the players. The werewolf wouldn't have much mechanical advantage to gathering a cult. Werewolves can move through humans without being noticed for the most part. The real need for a cult is more of an emotional need for people that aren't werewolves that are willing to accept the werewolf without running away in terror. That also comes with a lot of dangers, which is why they're so rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T18:45:50-08:00","id":23440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/23260-cult-of-the-werewolf?p=23261#post23261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blasphemies has a chapter on cults, including cults devoted to werewolves, I should note, and some packs and wolf-blooded families are essentially cults themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Cough*Pikerings*Cough*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T09:36:24-08:00","id":23802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RisTigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/23260-cult-of-the-werewolf?p=23357#post23357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have to look it up to see if that's accurate (or someone could tell me). But yes that would be very exploitable by the players. The werewolf wouldn't have much mechanical advantage to gathering a cult. Werewolves can move through humans without being noticed for the most part. The real need for a cult is more of an emotional need for people that aren't werewolves that are willing to accept the werewolf without running away in terror. That also comes with a lot of dangers, which is why they're so rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean Lunacy here? Because I don't think that a cultist would be more resilient to its effect than a werewolf hunter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T09:59:51-08:00","id":23811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/23260-cult-of-the-werewolf?p=23440#post23440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *Cough*Pikerings*Cough*</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, they are just a Hillbilly Family is all, albeit a very LARGE hillbilly family. No cult there, move along. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Keep the Faith","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T14:48:50-08:00","id":23989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/23260-cult-of-the-werewolf?p=23802#post23802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean Lunacy here? Because I don't think that a cultist would be more resilient to its effect than a werewolf hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant getting essence from cultists actually. I looked it up in the core, and it says essence can be harvested from doing rituals, but that it's only if werewolves are doing it.<br /> <br /> Yeah cultists would need the willpower to resist the lunacy which is another reason a werewolf cult would be rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T14:59:54-08:00","id":23993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RisTigger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/23260-cult-of-the-werewolf?p=23989#post23989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant getting essence from cultists actually. I looked it up in the core, and it says essence can be harvested from doing rituals, but that it's only if werewolves are doing it</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bit in Territories about how large outpourings of emotion can be used as temporary loci, too, mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:08:05-08:00","id":24755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/23260-cult-of-the-werewolf?p=23993#post23993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a bit in Territories about how large outpourings of emotion can be used as temporary loci, too, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait...what? Got a page for me on that? Sounds pretty incredible to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T18:18:14-08:00","id":24809,"title":"","content":"p32<br /> <br /> Raw Essence<br /> Spirits, Uratha and others attuned to magical energies may harvest Essence directly from massive outpourings of emotion from humans. The emotion must be similar for most or all humans in the area, and must be intense. Generally speaking, a great well of emotion from a human crowd acts as a \u201ctemporary locus\u201d of sorts. Essence comes into being in its rawest state, ready to be harvested by any spirits, werewolves or other entities quick enough to catch it. Spirits may even be able to cross the Gauntlet at the climax of the event \u2014 an \u201cangel\u201d manifesting before a crowd desperate to believe, or a spirit slipping into the material world to Ride an angry young rioter. Werewolves suffer a \u20133 penalty to die rolls made to harvest the Essence, as the timing is more challenging than drawing off Essence from a fixed locus.<br /> <br /> The event will generate roughly two Essence per dot of the event\u2019s intensity, which can be harvested in the usual fashion. The Storyteller is the final arbiter of any event\u2019s intensity, the following are merely guidelines. Note that the intensity of the event can be diluted or heightened by context. A snake-handling church in a region with many other such churches is less likely to generate Essence than one that operates in an area where such practices of faith are considerably rarer and more alarming. Note that certain events may trigger multiple such temporary loci, a city that breaks out in riots will probably have several separate riot events throughout the area, and a public assassination captured on television may spawn minor loci from people watching in large groups. <br /> <br /> * Particularly moving speech or theatrical performance, violent car accident on a freeway<br /> ** Major tent revival or other religious practice, dramatic moment during a sports game (last-minute, game-winning goal, for instance)<br /> *** Particularly damaging fire, act of random violence in a public place<br /> **** Riot, public assassination<br /> ***** Catastrophe or act of major violence, widespread panic or fury<br /> <br /> The Essence resonates with the emotions going on in the crowd (a riot\u2019s Essence is violent, a sports team\u2019s fans\u2019 Essence is exultant or despairing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T19:23:38-08:00","id":24843,"title":"","content":"Alright so how I'm not very good with the mechanics of the World of Darkness. So if any of this is off...well that's why. I would appreciate a quick looking over to see if anything's off or down right wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A werewolf cult is small, with the werewolf at the center acting as spiritual leader. The goal of the cult leader is to guide their followers in the ways of the spirits and teach them about the greater cosmology around them. In exchange, the cultists provide their service to their patron wolf. There also comes a great benefit to the werewolf leader. The leader can try and whip their cultists into a gathering of spirits and ritual. The great outpouring of emotions from their cultists can generate essence similar to that of a loci that can be harvested. If the emotions of the cultists are strong enough, the temporary locus provides essence to the werewolf leader and only the leader. Any other werewolf participating in the ritual cannot harvest this essence. But this outpouring of emotion also draws spirits into the physical world just like a locus.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The ritual to summon the valuable essence provides one essence for each cultist participating. However, the werewolf takes a -3 penalty to their Harmony Roll to harvest the essence generated from their revelry because they need to focus on ensuring the ritual goes smoothly. The ritual will generate an extra two essence if the cultists are under an influence that allows their minds to become more open to the Shadow. This can include psychotropic drugs from the Shadow. These sorts of rituals cannot be performed daily, as it\u2019s very taxing on the cultists and the leader, and they can only be performed every week. There are risks though, as the spirits nearby get a +2 bonus to pass through the Gauntlet. Sometimes this is part of the ritual as one of the goals is to summon a spirit the werewolf knows. But evil spirits can also pass through the Gauntlet. So performing the ritual in succession will increase these chances.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T23:12:18-08:00","id":25619,"title":"","content":"Also, what would a werewolf be like if he joined a cult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A werewolf in a cult is a powerful advantage. A raging bestial monster with knowledge of ghosts and spirits is someone that needs to be culled for the cause. But what kind of werewolf would even join a cult? A werewolf traditionally has a pack to lean on for support. In a word, stability. The constant and endless battle with spirits is trying on a normal mind. When you\u2019re being is split between two worlds, the damage to your psyche causes it to become fragile unless. So a vulnerable werewolf could easily be swayed by a charismatic soul. A soul that brings a sense of community without the need for fighting over status or territory. There\u2019s no young upstart urhara trying to vie for alpha status. Or an old wolf with no regard for others trying to order you around. All you need to do is provide support for the cause and you will be accepted.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">However, having a werewolf be a member of your cult comes with risks. A werewolf is a beast at heart and can become unpredictable if pushed to their limit. The werewolf also cannot be seen in its other forms, lest the members of the congregation be exposed to the lunacy that can damage their fragile minds. You don\u2019t want your people to be harmed by your ultimate weapon of the cause. The werewolf also brings danger from the Shadow. Strange spirits seeking to conquer a werewolf separated from its pack. That could utterly destroy your cult and bring about more problems from your other rivals seeing that you\u2019ve been weakened somehow. But despite all the risks a werewolf in an invaluable ally for a young cult. A werewolf brings a strength that no cultist can match. </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/410-ristigger","name":"RisTigger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar410_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}